#DESCRIPTION
Hybrid PIC (kinetic ions / fluid electrons) Proton Cyclotron Anisotropy
Instability (PCAI) wave test.

1D-3V: the ion temperature is anisotropic (bi-Maxwellian) with
  T_perp/T_par = 3, beta_par = 1,
so the plasma exceeds the proton-cyclotron anisotropy instability threshold
  P_perp/P_par - 1 ~ S / beta_par^0.4   (S ~ 1)
and a left-hand circularly-polarized (Alfven/ion-cyclotron) wave grows parallel
to the guide field at the linear-theory rate gamma/Omega_ci = 0.162.  This
validates the hybrid solver's capture of an electromagnetic anisotropy
instability driven by ion free energy (no net current / beam).

The anisotropic distribution is seeded by the WAVEIC anisoTPerpOverTPar option:
the UNIFORMSTATE temperature T is interpreted as the PARALLEL temperature T_par,
and the WaveIC thermal-velocity hook inflates the two components perpendicular
to the guide field (x) by sqrt(T_perp/T_par) = sqrt(3), reproducing the
Hybrid-VPIC reference seeding (ux~N(0,vthipar), uy,uz~N(0,vthiperp)).  A small
transverse (B_y, B_z) wave at the box-fundamental mode (frac = 0.02, just above
the ~1% thermal-noise floor) is seeded so the most-unstable mode is measured
cleanly; the linear growth rate is unchanged by the seed.  The growth rate is
measured from the total transverse-field norm sqrt(sum(By^2)) / sqrt(sum(Bz^2))
in tests/pcai/validate.py, matching the reference diagnostic.

Normalization matches hybrid_whistler: lNormSI = d_i, uNormSI = v_A, so
  d_i ~ 1, v_A ~ 1, B = Omega_ci ~ 1 in code units.
Physical inputs are solar-wind-like: n = 5 /cc, B = 5.125 nT, v_A ~ 50 km/s,
T_par ~ 1.5e5 K (beta_par = 1), T_perp = 3 T_par.

The box is Lx = 10.5 d_i (per the reference test: Lx/d_i = 10.5), 64 cells, so
dx = 0.164 d_i and the box-fundamental wavenumber k d_i = 2*pi/10.5 = 0.598 lies
in the unstable band of the parallel proton-cyclotron mode; the box contains ONE
wavelength of the growing mode (waveMode = 1), matching the reference.  dt*Omega_ci
= 0.01 matches the reference (dt = 0.02 s here).  Run for taui = 60 gyro-periods
(T_code = 60, TimeMax = 120 s) with fields saved every 20 steps (fields_interval
= 20 in pcai.cxx), following the Hybrid-VPIC setup.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-5.25                   xMin  [code units; Lx = 10.5 d_i]
 5.25                   xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

Standard Maxwell/GMRES solver disabled; use the Ohm's-law + Faraday hybrid
field advance instead.
#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

#AVGFIELDB
F                       useAvgFieldB
20                      nAvgFieldB

useAvgFieldB = F disables FLEKS's EMA time-averaging of B.  The Hybrid-VPIC
reference uses no B time-averaging (and no smoothing: nsub=1, nsm=0, eta=0,
damp=NULL); disabling the EMA matches the reference setup.

Resistivity OFF (0.0): the instability is driven purely by the ion temperature
anisotropy, so no extra dissipation is added.
#RESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaResistivity  [m^2/s, SI magnetic diffusivity]

Warm massless fluid electrons with T_e = T_par (13.06 eV = 151400 K), adiabatic
index gamma = 5/3, matching the Hybrid-VPIC reference (Te = Tipar = 0.5 in
mi*v_A^2 units).  Diagnostic found cold electrons (Te = 0) DO NOT produce the
instability (the n=1 mode just oscillates), while warm electrons, whose
pressure-gradient term couples to the parallel density perturbation of the
parallel proton-cyclotron mode, DO drive the growth -- consistent with the
reference.
#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
13.06                   electronTemperature  [eV]  (T_e = T_par)
1.6667                  electronGamma             (5/3)
1.0                     electronDensity0

Charge-density floor for the 1/rho factors in the Hall term and the
electron-pressure-gradient term.  Hybrid-VPIC clamps rho at max(rho, 0.05) in
its field advance (hyb_advance_e.cc), while FLEKS defaults to 1e-6; raising the
floor to the reference value prevents (J x B)/rho and grad(Pe)/rho from blowing
up if the density dips locally in the high-amplitude nonlinear phase.
#DENSITYFLOOR
0.05                    rhoFloorHybrid

Sub-cycle the B update.  FLEKS's hybrid discretization requires sub-cycling for
linear stability at the grid-scale (nsub = 1, as in Hybrid-VPIC, is linearly
unstable here), so we sub-cycle the Hall-whistler term.  The rk4 integrator
below uses the time-centred E (J from curl(B_stage), Hall/convection B from
(B_stage+B^n)/2) matching Hybrid-VPIC, which is stable in the high-amplitude
phase without over-damping the instability.
#HALLSUBCYCLE
32                      nHallSubcycle

Time-integration for the hybrid Faraday (B) update.  "rk4" now evaluates E at
the TIME-CENTRED B (B_stage + B^n)/2 in the generalized Ohm's law at each stage,
exactly as Hybrid-VPIC's hyb_advance_e uses (cbx+cbx0)/2 (B_n is stored by
STOREBOLD).  With nHallSubcycle = 1 this reproduces the Hybrid-VPIC field
advance (RK4, no sub-cycling), which is stable in the high-amplitude nonlinear
phase without over-damping the instability.
#FIELDINTEGRATOR
rk4                     fieldIntegrator

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
151400.0                T [K]        T_par (beta_par = 1, v_A = 5e4 m/s)
5.125e-9                bx [T]       uniform guide field Bx0 (B_code ~ 1)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TESTCASE
hybridwave

#WAVEIC
1                       waveMode            box-fundamental unstable mode
0.02                    frac                B perturbation amplitude
3.0                     anisoTPerpOverTPar  T_perp/T_par anisotropy ratio

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt            dt*Omega_ci = 0.01

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
5.0e4                   uNormSI   [m/s] ~ v_A so v_A ~ 1 in code units

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
10                      dnSavePic
10                      dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
5000                    nParticle per cell in X
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#COMOVING
F                       solvePartInCoMov
0                       nSmoothBackGroundU

#UPWINDE
F                       useUpwindE
0.0                     limiterThetaE

#UPWINDB
F                       doSmoothB
0.0                     theta

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
20                      dn
-1                      dt
1                       dx

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
120.0                   TimeMax      ~60 ion gyro-periods (taui = 60 wci^-1, matching Hybrid-VPIC pcai.cxx)

#RUN
